# CLAUDE.md — RentEase

## Project Overview

**RentEase** is a two-way boarding house rental matching platform built with Flutter and Firebase, targeting boarding house tenants and owners in Davao City, Philippines. It is a capstone research project by Dumadapat, Item, and Samson at the University of Mindanao.

The system's core contribution is a **dual-sided constraint-based filtering engine** combined with **TOPSIS multi-criteria ranking**, implemented as two separate single-sided instances — one ranking properties for tenants, one ranking tenants for owners. Communication between parties is only enabled after bilateral compatibility is confirmed.

---

## Architecture

### Stack
- **Frontend:** Flutter (Dart) — cross-platform mobile (Android/iOS)
- **State management:** BLoC (business logic) + Cubit (simpler states)
- **Backend:** Firebase
  - Firebase Authentication — login, signup, email verification, role-based access
  - Cloud Firestore — NoSQL document database (real-time)
  - ~~Cloud Functions~~ — **NOT USED.** Paid Firebase feature (requires Blaze plan); the project stays on the free Spark plan
  - ~~Firebase Cloud Messaging (FCM)~~ — **NOT USED.** Not part of this project's scope; no push notifications
  - **Note:** The project does not use Cloud Functions or FCM. Do not add them, suggest them, or write code that depends on them. Any other section of this file that refers to Cloud Functions (bilateral filter, TOPSIS, distance) or push notifications is superseded by this note; the matching/ranking logic must run without Cloud Functions (e.g., in the Flutter data/domain layer or via Firestore-only approaches), and notifications are in-app only (Firestore-backed Activity tab).
  - Firebase Storage — property photos, verification documents
- **Location:** Google Maps SDK for Flutter — map display and pin placement only
- **Distance:** `latlong2` package — computed from stored geographic coordinates, NOT via Maps Distance Matrix API

### Pattern
Clean Architecture with feature-first folder structure. Each feature has its own data, domain, and presentation layers. Shared widgets live in `lib/shared/widgets/`.

### Folder Structure
```
lib/
├── main.dart
├── app.dart
├── core/
│   ├── constants/
│   │   ├── app_colors.dart       ← single source of truth for all colors
│   │   ├── app_strings.dart
