## Absolute Rules — Never Violate

### 1. No Hardcoded Colors
```dart
// ❌ NEVER
Container(color: Color(0xFF1ABCCE))
// ✅ ALWAYS
Container(color: AppColors.primary)
```

### 2. Send Inquiry and Invite Buttons Must Be Absent When B_score = 0
```dart
// ❌ WRONG — disabled is not acceptable
AppButton(label: 'Send inquiry', isEnabled: false)

// ✅ CORRECT — completely absent
if (property['bScore'] == 1)
  AppButton(label: 'Send inquiry', onPressed: _sendInquiry)
else
  const SizedBox.shrink()
```

### 3. Session Filter State Never Writes to Firestore
Session filter overrides are local `StatefulWidget` state only. They reset on screen dispose. They never persist. They never write to `tenantProfiles` or any Firestore collection.

### 4. Role is Permanent
A user's role (tenant/owner) cannot be changed after signup. Do not add any UI that allows role switching.

### 5. Owner Cannot Post Listings Before Admin Approval
Firebase security rules must enforce `isVerified = true` before any property write is permitted. Do not rely on UI-only enforcement.

### 6. TOPSIS Runs on the Tenant's Device
There are no Cloud Functions. The tenant's device computes TOPSIS Ci in memory in the domain layer (`TopsisService`), never in widget code, from the tenant's eligible matches and the live property docs Home already loads. `tenantCi` / `tenantRank` are written back to the match docs only when the tenant's set of eligible matches changes. A ranking-only match update skips the eligibility re-check in `firestore.rules`, since Ci grants no access.

### 7. Full Matching Runs at Profile-Save Time; App Open Runs Only a Delta Check
- **Full scan** (all available listings) runs only when the tenant completes onboarding or saves their profile or preferences. It writes only changed outcomes: create newly eligible matches, set `bScore = 0` on matches no longer eligible, and never delete match docs that don't exist. It then stores `lastMatchedAt` (the newest listing `updatedAt` seen, i.e. server time) in `tenantProfiles/{uid}/private/prefs`.
- **App open** runs a delta check: `properties where updatedAt > lastMatchedAt − 2 minutes, orderBy updatedAt, limit 100`, paged. It scores only those listings, writes only changed outcomes, then advances `lastMatchedAt`. With no `lastMatchedAt` yet, it runs one full scan.
- **Unavailable listings** get no match write. They are filtered out at read time (Home, TOPSIS, owner screens) and reappear when available again. A match whose listing was deleted is deleted when Home finds it.
- **Every property write must stamp `updatedAt` with server time** (enforced in `firestore.rules`), otherwise existing tenants never see the change.
- Pull-to-refresh and the Search tab never trigger a full scan.
- **Limitation:** matches update only on the tenant's own device, so a tenant who doesn't open the app isn't matched to new listings until they do.

### 8. Admin Has No Self-Registration
Admin accounts are created manually in Firebase console. There is no sign-up flow for admin. The admin login screen has no "Create account" link.

